title Two ships, one guard, and a reach of 19 in 274
prompt THE BATON -- petrichor's autonomous lap. Baton, card, rota, thread, then the next agent-doable work in the docs-geode and prose lane under reds-first.

rota lap N was 4074 at the open by git rev-list --count HEAD, so N mod 5 is row 4 -- EARTH, which my own previous lap read at 133554. Advanced by hand to row 0, AETHER, Jupiter, why the work exists, sense of sound. Read the threshold and all three seats: Follow Our Compass, the Lindy Effect and the Long Return, the Grain and the Crossing. The strand seated at the fusion named this lap before it had a subject -- a guard that cannot red guards nothing, and a witness must be proven able to make a sound before its silence means anything. This lap found the sharper form: a guard that CAN red, DOES red, and is deaf to 93% of its own subject.

think Cold roster open, scoped: 120 guards, 113 green, 4 red, 3 gated, 1018s, tree_moved=no. Two of the four reds shared one root and it was in my lane -- construction/ITINERARY.md linked archive/REDS-...-rows-492.md and the shelf on disk is rows-494.md. readme_reach gates broken living links; reds_fold_witness duty 3 calls the same scan, so one absent target reddened two rostered guards.
think Traced rather than guessed: 4cc3eb0d0 added the shelf as rows-492, b441f97b2 renamed it to rows-494, and 4ae9c6130 was %495's repair at 14:09:17. Its diff shows the shape -- the block had read %492 above rows-492, agreeing and both stale, and the repair rewrote the PROSE number to %494 and left the link, so it consumed the very number-against-link disagreement %495's own what-caught-it names.
think Measured the class before building. First reading took the number from a window of prose before the link: 30 disagreements, 28 of them false, because a recital line carries several %NNN from earlier sentences. Tightened to anchored shapes: 57 citations, 55 landing, 2 disagreeing -- and both survivors RESOLVED, opening real shelves that were the wrong shelves.
think Built the guard, ran it green, committed, and fetched before the send. Upstream had moved six commits and one was b3307a57e, "read a citation's number against the path beside it" -- the same guard, by a peer, committed at 14:59:07 against my 14:56:19. They also booked %502 for it, and %500 through %502 were all taken while I worked.
think Theirs published first, so mine is withdrawn whole. That is %484's own precedent applied to me: one defect belongs to one record, and a second meter over one quantity is how two meters come to disagree. Parked my two commits at refs/heads/pier/petrichor-20260906-145718 so nothing is stranded -- %479's dead-letter lesson -- then reset to xy/main.
think Then asked the one question worth asking after a withdrawal: what does the survivor actually read. Their scan reads two promise shapes, an anchor that IS the number and an anchor carrying the word shelf. Measured independently and then confirmed with their own census: 274 links into a fold shelf stand in living files, and it reads 19.
think The largest population is the fold recital's own 47 lines, Row N folded to followed by a path-anchored link with a bare number. NUMBERED skips it because the anchor is a path; SHELF skips it because there is no shelf word. And nothing counted them -- shelf_unnumbered reads 0, which a reader takes as "every link carries a number and all agree" when it means "of the 19 I can see."
think So the lap became an extension inside their guard rather than a replacement beside it: the FOLD form anchored to the words immediately before the link exactly as their SHELF form is, a range checked at both endpoints, plus all_links and unread_links so the reach is a number. Their 23 assertions all still pass; the pen is 33 now.

obs THE WITHDRAWAL WAS THE RIGHT CALL AND IT COST AN HOUR OF DUPLICATE BUILD. A 265-line scan, a 20-case pen and an 83-line witness, written twice in one hour by two ships that could not see each other working. The card asks three separate times whether an OPEN row should carry a claim, a seat and a stamp at START; this is that question with a price attached rather than a hypothesis, and it is the strongest evidence yet because what duplicated was not a row number but a whole instrument.
obs COMPARING TWO READINGS IS WORTH MORE THAN EITHER ALONE. Neither hand would have measured the other's reach; each would have shipped a green guard and believed it. Their two shapes see 19 of 274, mine saw 57 by a different cut, and the union with the reach printed sees 66 and names the 208 it cannot. The duplicate hour bought a measurement that a single build could not have produced.
obs A GUARD'S REACH IS A CLAIM, AND AN UNPRINTED REACH IS CLAIMED BY IMPLICATION. This is %451's class inside a guard one hour old, and it is not a criticism of the build -- their header is honest about reading two forms and stops there. What was missing is the number, and a census that prints only what it gates reads as though it covered the room.
obs THE SIGNED SUBTRACTION IS %498'S LESSON TAKEN FIRST-HAND. unread_links is all_links minus the three read counts, kept signed, so a link matching two shapes at once refuses by name rather than clamping to a comfortable zero. A count that cannot go below zero cannot tell you it is wrong.
obs I WROTE THE SAME FALSE LINK TWICE IN ONE LAP. My withdrawn row illustrated the recital shape in live bracket-paren syntax, and readme_reach reddened on it. I named that in the row as the placeholder law's fourth firing -- and then did it again in the replacement row, on the very sentence describing the shape. Fifth firing, twice under a hand actively writing about links. The loom exists and caught both within a minute; what no loom reaches is the keystroke.
obs A PEER ALSO FOLDED %491 THIRTY-ONE MINUTES AHEAD OF ME, onto a different shelf name, at 20260906.141608 against my 145226. Withdrawn the same way. Three withdrawals in one lap -- a fold, a guard, and a row -- all by the same rule, and every one cheap because the fetch came before the send rather than after it.
obs THE CARD HALF OF THE ORIGINAL REPAIR FIXED ITSELF. A peer's unrelated round removed the broken target at 8e227fe95, 22 minutes after %495 closed and without naming it, so my identical repair merged away to nothing. The two links that RESOLVE were repaired by the peer's guard round rather than by mine. The visible half attracts hands; the invisible half waits for an instrument.
obs THE DEAD-END NUMBER IS MEASURED AND UNTOUCHED BY ANY OF THIS. Of 607 living pages a newcomer reaches from README.md, 82 lead nowhere -- 13.5%, of which 76 carry no link syntax at all. By room: gratitude 23, classical-vedic-astrology 21, .claude/rules 15, construction/archive 8, scribble/fixtures 6, context 4, and one tutorial on my own shelf, docs-geode/tutorials/recursion-in-glow.md, which cites seven paths in backticks and links none. Six of the 82 are parser fixtures and are data rather than pages.

loom guard=reds_citation before_reach=19 after_reach=66 all_links=274 unread=208 fold_links=47 cases=33
loom roster=cold_open_scoped guards=120 green=113 red=4 gated=3 wall_s=1018
loom roster=hot_pass guards=150 green=141 red=5 gated=4 wall_s=1323
loom census=front_door_dead_ends living_pages=607 dead_end=82 no_links_at_all=76 external_only=6

file tools/fixtures/r/reds_citation_scan.sh the FOLD form read as a third promise, and all_links beside unread_links so the reach is counted
file tools/fixtures/r/reds_citation_control.sh ten cases added -- the fold from both sides, its range endpoints, the unread count, and the reach identity
file tools/r/reds_citation_witness.rish fold_disagree gated, the reach asserted present, the corpus asserted non-empty
file construction/REDS.md row %505, booked after a fetch; the number moved four times before it landed
file construction/ITINERARY.md the Petrichor block, the Git nib at HEAD, the landed row

recommend kg -- the extended guard names 208 living shelf links it still cannot check, and the honest next lap is to read a sample of them and say which are promises wearing a fourth shape and which are prose that names a row without claiming it. That number is the guard's own reach and it is the only figure standing between a green and a claim of coverage. The dead-end census keeps its number, 82 of 607, and its floor waits on Keaton's word.
